    <briefdescription>
<para>Unary predicate struct template. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Derived from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1unary__op_1a5403004d70e9dd8508698e33cf412e95" kindref="member">unary_op</ref></computeroutput>, this struct checks a property of a single operand, using the predicate defined by the tag <computeroutput>Predicate_T</computeroutput>, and reports the symbol of the tag followed by the operand upon failure, as <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1not__op" kindref="compound">not_op</ref></computeroutput> reports <computeroutput>not</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>It is public, as <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1predicate__op" kindref="compound">extension::predicate_op</ref></computeroutput>, so that the applications can define their own predicates with their own tags. A tag is an empty struct with:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>a <computeroutput>static constexpr const char* symbol</computeroutput>, written before the operand in the failure reports, with the trailing space (for example <computeroutput>"even "</computeroutput>);</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>a static <computeroutput>apply (<ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1unary__op_1a1c076678ac794ab6216dd967496dd904" kindref="member">operand</ref>)</computeroutput> member function template, which receives the unwrapped operand (the value of a <computeroutput>to_*</computeroutput> wrapper or of a literal) and returns the result as <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The tag is passed as an empty constructor argument, so that both template arguments are deduced, for example <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1predicate__op" kindref="compound">predicate_op</ref>{ <ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1value" kindref="compound">value</ref>, even{} }</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>The operand is not copied: a temporary is moved into the predicate, and a named operand of class type is referred to (see <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a85cd019d0861a4b6d62c3424f4a8931d" kindref="member">stored_operand_t</ref></computeroutput>). A predicate built in a function from its <computeroutput>const&amp;</computeroutput> parameter refers to the argument of that function, so it must be checked in the statement that calls the function.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored operand, either the operand type, or a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> reference to it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Predicate_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The tag that defines the predicate. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
